AB  - AI coding agents can solve a large fraction of real-world software engineering tasks, yet the complexity and maintainability of their patches remain poorly understood and largely uncontrolled. We present Wily v2, a high-performance code-analysis tool that computes code complexity at over 570000 LOC/s, and integrate it as a complexity backpressure signal inside an agentic coding harness. To evaluate Wily on substantive tasks, we construct SWE-bench Complex, a dataset of 116 real GitHub issues from major Python projects with a median patch size of 48 lines (6.9× SWE-bench Verified). We evaluated three frontier models under control and Wily-feedback conditions. A single round of Wily feedback significantly reduces cyclomatic complexity by 20–31% and cognitive complexity by 39–54% across all three models.
