AB  - This paper presents a collaborative multi-agent framework for autonomous code generation and debugging. By leveraging frameworks like LangGraph and CrewAI, specialized agents—including programmers, reviewers, and testers interact dynamically to enhance correctness and efficiency. These systems integrate tool enabled LLMs to access external APIs, execute tests, and iteratively refine code, addressing the limitations of single models in complex software tasks. Benchmarks reveal that while LLMs excel in pattern matching, multi-agent collaboration significantly improves performance in repo-level programming and bug resolution. Emerging approaches featuring graph-based coordination and self-debugging loops demonstrate the potential for self-evolving agent networks. However, challenges in scalability and robustness necessitate hybrid human-AI workflows. This collaborative framework represents a paradigm shift from single-model synthesis towards autonomous, end-to-end software development.
