AB  - The new era in software engineering is evolving with the rise of AI agents. AI agents are changing the thought process of architecting industry applications. AI agents provide several benefits that are better than traditional software solutions. There is a need for a standard business model to help design a variety of software products that leverage AI agents. This research presents a new business model, “AI Agents as a Service” (AIAaaS). It would act as a ready reference for building various applications with AI agents. The complete architecture of AIAaaS, with working and the intention of including every block in it, is discussed in depth. Using the proposed model, software products and applications could be deployed in the cloud, on-premise, edge and hybrid setups. The IT helpdesk use case was implemented and the results across three models, viz. baseline (manual), LLM only (SaaS) and Agentic AI (AIAaaS), are compared. The results of AIAaaS demonstrate 69% reduction in human efforts and 67.5% cost reduction compared to other baseline implementations. First Contact Resolution is increased by 40% and latency is reduced by 84.78% compared to baseline. From the results, it is found that AIAaaS can be used effectively to improve accuracy and reliability, keeping Human-In-Loop whenever required. This change can boost the efficiency and effectiveness of traditional systems.
