AB  - With the ever-increasing complexity of modern software systems, maintenance, improvement, and refactoring of code, as well as testing and documentation, have become increasingly labor-intensive and error-prone. Though various developer tools have been developed to provide partial assistance in this regard, they still largely remain passive and lack true autonomy in their capabilities. This paper describes an intelligent agentic system to provide true autonomy in codebase improvement and maintenance. The intelligent agentic system, as described in this paper, is based on a modular agent structure to perform various code improvement and maintenance tasks in a coordinated manner. The intelligent agentic system also combines the benefits of code analysis and contextual reasoning with memory to provide coherence in code improvement and maintenance. The intelligent agentic system has been tested using various code quality, test coverage, and developer effort metrics using actual codebases. The results of the experiment have shown promise in using agentic systems to provide true autonomy in code improvement and maintenance.
