AB  - To address the critical challenge of increasing token consumption of Large Language Models (LLMs), this study proposes a framework called Smart Cascade which combines trajectory reduction with model cascading. In this framework, when the lightweight model (Qwen 2.5 Coder 1.5B) task fails, it is compressed and transferred to the expensive model (Mistral 7B). This approach differs from conventional approach such as Standard Cascade where the entire failed output is passed. The proposed framework was evaluated on the HumanEval benchmark (164 tasks) under 4-bit quantized inference. Smart Cascade attains a 59.76% Pass@1 recovery rate, representing a substantial leap from the 21.34% Mistral 7B single pass baseline. Furthermore, the framework reduces the total weighted inference cost by 15.54% with no significant latency overhead. The findings here confirm structured diagnostic summarization can serve as an effective approach to optimization of cascaded LLM inference, thus maintaining task accuracy.
