AB  - This paper proposes an Autonomous Code Refactor and Documentation Agent using Agentic AI, a system that combines code refactoring and automated documentation into one independent framework. Different from the traditional architecture of isolated AI-assisted programming tools, the proposed architecture adopts a multi-agent collaboration model, in which each agent specializes in certain tasks and coordinates with others via a shared reasoning environment. The Refactor Agent autonomously analyses source code, checks structural inefficiencies, and then performs refactoring while preserving the context independently, while the Documentation Agent interprets the changes made to the code and forms human-understandable descriptions that are compatible with software engineering standards. The resulting framework can achieve a high degree of autonomy, reduced human supervision, and comprehensibility by synchronized code enhancements and explanations. This study establishes the grounds for future agentic AI systems integrating intelligent reasoning, collaboration, and explainability into the software development process.
