AB  - Large language model (LLM) based agents have demonstrated strong potential for automating data science workflows, with DS-Agent combining LLM reasoning with case-based reasoning (CBR) grounded in Kaggle expert solutions. However, DS-Agent applies a single LLM uniformly across all internal roles regardless of their differing complexity and its evaluation relies exclusively on proprietary models such as GPT-4 and GPT-3.5. This study proposes a manually designed role-aware hybrid LLM configuration that assigns DeepSeek-R1, a reasoning-specialized model to the high-complexity Planner role, while deploying DeepSeek-V3 across the Programmer, Debugger, Logger and RankReviser roles. The configuration is evaluated alongside uniform DeepSeek-V3 and against GPT-4, the strongest baseline in the original DS-Agent benchmark, across 12 development tasks spanning natural language processing (NLP), time series and tabular domains, whose GPT-4 results are inherited under the same task set and ranking protocol. Uniform DeepSeek-V3 is the weakest of the three configurations. Replacing only its Planner with DeepSeek-R1 while retaining DeepSeek-V3 retained in every other role, produces the strongest: the hybrid outperforms GPT-4 on 7 of 12 tasks by best rank and 10 of 12 by mean rank, winning all four NLP tasks, at 0.0158 USD per run against 1.60 USD for GPT-4, a 99 percent reduction. Domain-level analysis shows that reasoning-specialized planning provides the greatest advantage on language-heavy tasks, while GPT-4 retains an edge on structured tabular data. For deployment, both DeepSeek configurations are evaluated on the original GPT-4 agent case bank, with DeepSeek-R1 as the Adapter outperforming DeepSeek-V3 on 15 of 18 tasks at 31 percent lower cost than GPT-4. These findings show that role-aware model assignment is a practical and cost-efficient strategy for open-source LLM deployment in automated data science pipelines. The code, experimental configurations and results are publicly available at https://github.com/muhammadhaider02/DS-Agent.
